    #chat-form { display: flex; }
    #user-input { flex: 1; margin-right: 5px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="chat"></div>
  <form id="chat-form">
    <input type="text" id="user-input" placeholder="Type your message...">
    <button type="submit">Send</button>
  </form>

  <!-- Include Transformers.js dependencies -->
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tensorflow/tfjs"></script>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@huggingface/tfjs-transformers"></script>

  <script>
    // JavaScript code will go here
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### 2. Add JavaScript Code
```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', async () => {
  const tokenizer = await Transformers.BlenderBotTokenizer.from_pretrained('facebook/blenderbot-400M-distilled');
  const model = await Transformers.BlenderBotForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained('facebook/blenderbot-400M-distilled');

  const chatForm = document.getElementById('chat-form');
  const chatContainer = document.getElementById('chat');
  const userInput = document.getElementById('user-input');

  chatForm.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();

    // Get user message
    const userMessage = userInput.value.trim();
    if (!userMessage) return;

    // Clear input after sending
    userInput.value = '';

    // Display user message
    chatContainer.innerHTML += `<div class="user-message">You: ${userMessage}</div>`;
    chatContainer.scrollTop = chatContainer.scrollHeight;

    try {
      // Encode user message
      const inputs = tokenizer.encode(userMessage);

      // Generate response
      const outputs = await model.generate(inputs, { max_length: 50 });
      const botResponse = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0].arraySync()).trim();

      // Display bot response
      chatContainer.innerHTML += `<div class="bot-message">Bot: ${botResponse}</div>`;
      chatContainer.scrollTop = chatContainer.scrollHeight;
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error generating response:', error);
      chatContainer.innerHTML += `<div class="error">Error: ${error.message}</div>`;
    }
  });
});
```

### 3. Explanation of Key Components
1. **Dependencies**
   - `@tensorflow/tfjs`: TensorFlow.js core library
   - `@huggingface/tfjs-transformers`: Transformers.js library from Hugging Face

2. **Model Initialization**
   ```javascript
   Transformers.BlenderBotTokenizer.from_pretrained(...)
   Transformers.BlenderBotForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(...)
   ```
   Loads the tokenizer and model from Hugging Face's Model Hub

3. **Chat Handling**
   - User message submission is handled via form submission
   - Messages are displayed in a scrollable chat window
   - Model processes input using:
     1. Tokenization: Turns text into token IDs
     2. Generation: Uses model to create response
     3. Decoding: Turns token IDs back into text

4. **Error Handling**
   - Catches any errors during response generation
   - Displays error messages in the chat container

### 4. Customization Options
- **Styling**: Modify the CSS to change colors, fonts, and layout
- **Model Parameters**: Adjust generation parameters like:
  ```javascript
  const outputs = await model.generate(inputs, { 
    max_length: 100,    // Maximum response length
    temperature: 0.8,   // Controls randomness (0 = deterministic, 1 = more creative)
    num_beams: 5        // Number of beams for beam search
  });
  ```
- **Input Handling**: Add input validation or history tracking
- **UI Enhancements**: Add loading spinners or typing indicators

### 5. How to Test
1. Save the HTML file with the included JavaScript
2. Open in a modern browser (Chrome/Firefox recommended)
3. Type messages and press Enter to get responses
4. The model will maintain conversation context automatically

### Notes:
- The model takes ~10-15 seconds to load initially
- Longer messages may take longer to process
- The model works best for conversational dialogue
- For production use, consider adding error retries and better error handling

This creates a basic yet functional chat interface that maintains conversation context using the BlenderBot model. You can expand this by adding features like message history persistence or user authentication.

Here's a step-by-step guide to creating a circular radius slider with concentric markers using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        /* Container styling */
        .circular-slider {
            position: relative;
            width: 200px; /* 2 * maxRadius (100px) */
            height: 200px;
            display: inline-block;
        }

        /* Base circle and markers */
        .slider-circle {
            position: absolute;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            border: 2px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 50%;
        }

        /* Base circle (outermost) */
        .base {
            width: var(--radius);
            height: var(--radius);
        }

        /* Middle markers */
        .marker {
            --radius: 80px;
            border-color: #aaa;
            opacity: 0.5;
        }

        /* Inner marker */
        .marker:last-child {
            --radius: 60px;
        }

        /* Handle styling */
        .handle {
            position: absolute;
            width: 20px;
            height: 20px;
            background: #007bff;
            border-radius: 50%;
            cursor: pointer;
            z-index: 1;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            transition: background 0.2s;
        }

        /* Value display */
        .value-display {
            position: absolute;
            bottom: 10px;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translateX(-50%);
            color: #333;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="circular-slider" id="slider">
        <!-- Base circle -->
        <div class="slider-circle base" style="--radius: 100px;"></div>
        <!-- Middle marker -->
        <div class="slider-circle marker" style="--radius: 80px;"></div>
        <!-- Inner marker -->
        <div class="slider-circle marker" style="--radius: 60px;"></div>
        <!-- Handle -->
        <div class="handle"></div>
        <!-- Value display -->
        <div class="value-display">50</div>
    </div>

    <script>
        const slider = document.getElementById('slider');
        const handle = document.querySelector('.handle');
        const valueDisplay = document.querySelector('.value-display');

        let isDragging = false;
        let centerX, centerY, maxRadius, minRadius = 10;

        function init() {
            const rect = slider.getBoundingClientRect();

            // Calculate center coordinates
            centerX = rect.width / 2;
            centerY = rect.height / 2;

            // Get maximum radius (base circle radius)
            maxRadius = rect.width / 2 - 10; // Subtract 10 for handle padding

            // Set initial handle position (50% radius)
            const initialRadius = maxRadius * 0.5;
            const angle = 0; // Start along the positive x-axis
            handle.style.left = centerX + initialRadius * Math.cos(angle) + 'px';
            handle.style.top = centerY + initialRadius * Math.sin(angle) + 'px';

            setValueDisplay(initialRadius);

            // Add event listeners
            handle.addEventListener('mousedown', startDrag);
            handle.addEventListener('touchstart', startDrag);
            window.addEventListener('mouseup', endDrag);
            window.addEventListener('touchend', endDrag);
            window.addEventListener('mousemove', drag);
            window.addEventListener('touchmove', drag);
        }

        function startDrag(e) {
            isDragging = true;
            e.preventDefault();
        }

        function endDrag() {
            isDragging = false;
        }

        function drag(e) {
            if (!isDragging) return;

            // Get mouse/touch coordinates
            const rect = slider.getBoundingClientRect();
            let clientX = e.clientX || e.touches[0].clientX;
            let clientY = e.clientY || e.touches[0].clientY;

            // Calculate relative position from center
            const dx = clientX - rect.left - centerX;
            const dy = clientY - rect.top - centerY;

            let distance = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);

            // Clamp between min and max radius
            distance = Math.max(minRadius, Math.min(distance, maxRadius));

            // Calculate new position based on angle
            const angle = Math.atan2(dy, dx);
            const newX = centerX + distance * Math.cos(angle);
            const newY = centerY + distance * Math.sin(angle);

            // Update handle position
            handle.style.left = newX + 'px';
            handle.style.top = newY + 'px';

            // Update displayed value
            setValueDisplay(distance);
        }

        function setValueDisplay(value) {
            valueDisplay.textContent = Math.round(value).toString();
        }

        init();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Key Features:
1. **Circular UI**: 
   - The slider is a circle with concentric markers at 60%, 80%, and 100% of the maximum radius
   - The handle moves freely within the circle's area

2. **Drag-to-Adjust**: 
   - Users can drag the blue handle to any point within the circle
   - The current radius is calculated from the center to the handle's position

3. **Responsive Updates**: 
   - The displayed value updates in real-time as you drag the handle
   - Touch-friendly with mobile device support

4. **Styling Flexibility**: 
   - Easily customize marker colors and sizes through CSS
   - Adjust the minimum and maximum radii by modifying the `minRadius` and `maxRadius` variables

### Customization Options:
1. **Add More Markers**: 
   ```html
   <!-- Add another marker at 40% radius -->
   <div class="slider-circle marker" style="--radius: 40px;"></div>
   ```

2. **Change Colors**: 
   ```css
   .handle { background: #ff6b6b; } /* Red handle */
   .marker { border-color: #4CAF50; } /* Green markers */
   ```

3. **Adjust Radius Limits**: 
   ```javascript
   let minRadius = 20; // New minimum radius
   maxRadius = 90;     // New maximum radius
   ```

4. **Display Percentage Instead of Raw Value**:
   ```javascript
   function setValueDisplay(value) {
       const percentage = ((value / maxRadius) * 100).toFixed(0);
       valueDisplay.textContent = `${percentage}%`;
   }
   ```

### How It Works:
1. **Initialization**: 
   - Calculates the center and maximum radius when the page loads
   - Sets the initial handle position at 50% radius

2. **Event Handling**: 
   - `startDrag()` begins dragging when the handle is clicked
   - `drag()` continuously updates the handle position while dragging
   - `endDrag()` stops dragging when the mouse/touch is released

3. **Math Calculations**: 
   - Uses trigonometry to calculate the new position based on the mouse coordinates
   - Clamps the radius between specified min/max values

This implementation provides a smooth, intuitive interface for selecting a radius value through a circular slider. The markers improve user understanding of the scale and current selection.

