     2. Use `--stacktrace` or a debugger to trace the exact location of `Future.get()` in your code.

---

### Example of Proper Task Handling:
```java
ExecutorService executor = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();
Future<String> future = executor.submit(() -> {
    // Simulate a task.
    Thread.sleep(2000);
    return "Result";
});

try {
    // Cancel the task after 1 second.
    if (!future.get(1000, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS).isDone()) {
        future.cancel(true); // Cancel if it's still running.
    }
    // Safely retrieve the result.
    if (future.isDone()) {
        try {
            String result = future.get();
            System.out.println("Result: " + result);
        } catch (CancellationException e) {
            System.out.println("Task was canceled.");
        }
